# Context-Aware Agent Recipes

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:runic_ai, path: "~/wrk/runic_ai"}
])

Code.require_file("support/runic_ai_livebook.exs", __DIR__)
```

## Purpose

The context-aware recipes are for conversations where raw transcript history is
not enough. They combine focus inference, memory, retrieval, pressure handling,
prompt bundles, and optional tools.

This notebook looks at:

* `SummaryBackedChatAgent`: chat plus context engineering
* `MemoryAwareToolAgent`: context engineering plus tool calling
* `HandoffContextBuilder`: focused handoff artifacts for another thread or role

## Provider Setup

```elixir
setup = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.inputs()
```

```elixir
model = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_model!(setup)
llm_opts = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.llm_opts(model, max_output_tokens: RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_max_output_tokens(setup))
```

## Shared Context Inputs

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Memory.Entry
alias RunicAI.Retrieval.Document
alias RunicAI.Tool.Definition

memory_entries = [
  Entry.new!(
    kind: :semantic,
    content: "The customer prefers brief status updates and uses the project codename Lantern.",
    summary: "Customer prefers brief Lantern updates",
    salience: 0.9
  )
]

retrieval_docs = [
  Document.new!(
    id: "lantern-ops",
    content:
      "Lantern uses a staged rollout. If the health check fails, pause rollout and inspect the queue worker.",
    score: 0.9,
    metadata: %{title: "Lantern operations note"}
  )
]

status_tool =
  Definition.new!(
    name: "get_rollout_status",
    description: "Get demo rollout status for a project.",
    parameter_schema: [project: [type: :string, required: true]],
    executor: fn %{project: project} ->
      {:ok, %{project: project, rollout: "paused", reason: "health check failed"}}
    end
  )

single_tool_batch = RunicAI.Livebook.Tools.once_per_loop_selector()

Kino.Layout.tabs(
  Memory: Kino.Tree.new(memory_entries),
  Retrieval: Kino.Tree.new(retrieval_docs),
  Tool: Kino.Tree.new(status_tool)
)
```

## Summary-Backed Chat

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Recipes.SummaryBackedChatAgent

summary_workflow =
  SummaryBackedChatAgent.new(
    model: model,
    system: "Use available context. Say when a fact came from memory or retrieval.",
    memory_store: memory_entries,
    retrieval_provider: retrieval_docs,
    llm_opts: llm_opts
  )

RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(summary_workflow)
```

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.require_openai_key!()

summary_run =
  summary_workflow
  |> Runic.Workflow.react_until_satisfied(%{
    user: "Give me a brief Lantern rollout status summary."
  })

SummaryBackedChatAgent.latest_reply_text(summary_run)
```

## Memory-Aware Tool Agent

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Recipes.MemoryAwareToolAgent

tool_context_workflow =
  MemoryAwareToolAgent.new(
    model: model,
    system: "Use context and tools to answer operational questions.",
    memory_store: memory_entries,
    retrieval_provider: retrieval_docs,
    registry: [status_tool],
    tool_selector: single_tool_batch,
    tool_requirement: :required,
    llm_opts: llm_opts
  )

RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(tool_context_workflow)
```

```elixir
tool_context_run =
  MemoryAwareToolAgent.react_until_resolution(
    [
      model: model,
      system: "Use context and tools to answer operational questions.",
      memory_store: memory_entries,
      retrieval_provider: retrieval_docs,
      registry: [status_tool],
      tool_selector: single_tool_batch,
      tool_requirement: :required,
      llm_opts: llm_opts
    ],
    %{user: "Check Lantern and tell me what to do next."}
  )

MemoryAwareToolAgent.latest_reply_text(tool_context_run)
```

```elixir
Kino.Layout.tabs(
  Bundle: Kino.Tree.new(MemoryAwareToolAgent.latest_bundle(tool_context_run)),
  Tools: Kino.Tree.new(MemoryAwareToolAgent.latest_tool_results(tool_context_run)),
  State: Kino.Tree.new(MemoryAwareToolAgent.latest_state(tool_context_run))
)
```

## Interactive Context Tool Agent

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Chat.start(
  MemoryAwareToolAgent,
  [
    model: model,
    system: "Use context and tools to answer operational questions.",
    memory_store: memory_entries,
    retrieval_provider: retrieval_docs,
    registry: [status_tool],
    tool_selector: single_tool_batch,
    tool_requirement: :required,
    llm_opts: llm_opts
  ],
  initial_message: "What is happening with Lantern?"
)
```
